The peer's bandwidth allowance, ours (not whatsapp-light's); applied by scripts/hypermeow-work.sh after
meowcaller-group.patch. Android's WhatsApp sends RTCP PSFB FMT 15 "PRST" packets about every 5 s: the
bit/s it lets us send (rtp.BuildPrst writes the same packet; the engine never read the peer's).
1. rtp.ParsePrst finds the allowance in a compound RTCP packet, every length checked (rtcp_prst.go,
   with its test).
2. VideoAllowanceSink (video.go) is the optional interface a VideoSink may add, as
   VideoOrientationSink; runMedia calls SetAllowance with each PRST it reads, right after the RTCP
   census. The engine's video sink passes it to the UI's camera (calls_video.go).
